B.azd=new A.a4("How Stones ratings work\n\nEvery rated game updates Overall and its format ladder: board shape, size, player count, rules and clock category. Humans and shared AI profiles use the same uncertainty-aware Glicko-based system. Live standings include both. The winner beats every other seat. All other players receive a loss, without being ranked against one another. Larger games carry proportionally smaller loss penalties. A drawn game counts as a draw for everyone. Changes depend on skill estimates and uncertainty.\n\nProfiles show an approximate 95% skill range. It narrows as evidence accumulates and describes skill, not a range of leaderboard positions. Ratings are provisional for at least ten games and until uncertainty is sufficiently low. Equal established ratings share a rank.\n\nSigned-in players can record completed human, AI and mixed games. Online humans confirm the result. Guest games, learning, Court Mode, abandoned games and shared human seats are unrated. AI results are reported by the player\u2019s device. Player display names and competitive statistics are public. These are Stones ratings, not chess ratings.",null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null,null)
